---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /nav-concepts/
title: Navbar concepts
description: Prototype comparison of five navigation bars for the site.
robots: noindex, nofollow
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#
  Prototype page: five navbar treatments, each running live inside a small
  scrollable copy of the homepage (scroll inside a preview to see the
  scrolled state; switch to Phone to see the mobile version).
  Not linked from the site, kept out of the sitemap.
  Styles: nav-concepts.css · Behaviour: nav-concepts.js
#}
{%- set sections = [
  { id: "services", label: "Services" },
  { id: "studio", label: "The Studio" },
  { id: "gallery", label: "Gallery" },
  { id: "visit", label: "Visit" }
] -%}

{%- macro links(cls) -%}
{%- for s in sections %}<a href="#" data-go="{{ s.id }}"{% if cls %} class="{{ cls }}"{% endif %}>{{ s.label }}</a>{% endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro brand(extra) -%}
<a class="nc-brand {{ extra }}" href="#" data-go="top" aria-label="Rays Beauty Salon, home"><b>Rays</b><small>Beauty Salon</small></a>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro burger() -%}
<button class="nc-burger" type="button" data-menu-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu"><span></span><span></span></button>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro star(cls) -%}
<svg class="nc-star {{ cls }}" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 0C10.6 6.4 13.6 9.4 20 10 13.6 10.6 10.6 13.6 10 20 9.4 13.6 6.4 10.6 0 10 6.4 9.4 9.4 6.4 10 0Z"/></svg>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- A shortened homepage the navs sit over -#}
{%- macro demoPage() -%}
<div class="nc-page">
  <section class="nc-hero" data-sec="top">
    <div class="nc-hero__text">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Open &amp; welcoming · Cobourg</p>
      <p class="nc-hero__title">Hair &amp; <em>beauty</em><br />in the heart<br />of Cobourg.</p>
      <div class="nc-hero__actions">
        <a class="btn btn--teal btn--small" href="#" data-go="book">Book an appointment</a>
        <a class="link link--light" href="#" data-go="services">View services</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <img class="nc-hero__img" src="/assets/img/hero-portrait-1000.jpg" width="1000" height="1371" loading="lazy" alt="" />
  </section>

  <section class="nc-sec" data-sec="services">
    <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
    <p class="nc-h">The menu</p>
    <div class="nc-cards">
      {%- for c in [["cut", "Cut &amp; Style"], ["colour", "Colour"], ["styling", "Styling"], ["care", "Care"]] %}
      <div class="nc-card"><img src="/assets/img/services/{{ c[0] }}.jpg" width="933" height="1400" loading="lazy" alt="" /><span>{{ c[1] | safe }}</span></div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nc-sec nc-studio" data-sec="studio">
    <img src="/assets/img/studio-stylist-sm.jpg" width="924" height="1000" loading="lazy" alt="" />
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The Studio</p>
      <p class="nc-h">A quiet chair in the heart of town.</p>
      <p class="nc-mute">Rays is an intimate, unhurried salon. You'll be seen by name and never rushed, with one stylist from consultation to final mirror check.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nc-sec nc-gallery" data-sec="gallery">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Lookbook</p>
    <p class="nc-h">Recent work</p>
    <div class="nc-thumbs">
      {%- for f in ["windswept", "textured-lob", "soft-layers", "sun-kissed"] %}
      <img src="/assets/img/lookbook/{{ f }}-thumb.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="" />
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nc-sec nc-visit" data-sec="visit">
    <p class="eyebrow">Visit</p>
    <p class="nc-h">247 Division St, <em>Cobourg</em></p>
    <p class="nc-mute">Street parking out front · By appointment</p>
  </section>

  <section class="nc-sec nc-book" data-sec="book">
    <p class="nc-h">Book your <em>chair.</em></p>
    <span class="btn btn--light btn--small">Book an appointment</span>
  </section>

  <footer class="nc-foot">© Rays Beauty Salon</footer>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Toolbar + frame wrapper: caller() renders the concept's nav markup -#}
{%- macro stage(cls) -%}
<div class="nc-stage {{ cls }}" data-stage>
  <div class="nc-toolbar">
    <div class="nc-seg" role="group" aria-label="Preview size">
      <button type="button" data-device="desktop" aria-pressed="true">Desktop</button>
      <button type="button" data-device="phone" aria-pressed="false">Phone</button>
    </div>
    <span class="nc-hint">Scroll inside the preview ↓</span>
  </div>
  <div class="nc-frame" role="region" aria-label="Live preview">
    {{ caller() }}
    <div class="nc-scroller" data-scroller tabindex="0" aria-label="Preview page, scrollable">{{ demoPage() }}</div>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/nav-concepts.css" />

<header class="nc-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Prototype · not linked from the site</p>
    <h1 class="nc-head__title">The navbar, <em>five ways.</em></h1>
    <p class="nc-head__note">Each concept runs live over a short copy of the homepage. Scroll inside a preview to see how it changes past the hero, and switch to <strong>Phone</strong> to see the mobile menu.</p>
    <nav class="nc-head__jump" aria-label="Concepts">
      <a class="link link--light" href="#c1">1 · Shopfront</a>
      <a class="link link--light" href="#c2">2 · Glass capsule</a>
      <a class="link link--light" href="#c3">3 · Front desk</a>
      <a class="link link--light" href="#c4">4 · The index</a>
      <a class="link link--light" href="#c5">5 · Booking dock</a>
      <a class="link link--light" href="#compare">At a glance</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============ 1 · Shopfront ============ -->
<section class="nc-concept" id="c1" aria-labelledby="t1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nc-label">
      <span class="nc-label__tag">Concept 1</span>
      <h2 id="t1" class="nc-label__title">Shopfront</h2>
      <p class="nc-label__text">The wordmark moves to the centre like a sign over the door, links split either side with small stars, and Book sits at the far right. Past the hero the bar turns ivory and the wordmark shrinks. On a phone: menu on the left, Rays in the middle, Book on the right; the menu drops down from the top.</p>
    </div>
    {% call stage("n1") %}
    <header class="nc-nav">
      <div class="n1__bar">
        <div class="n1__side n1__side--l">
          {{ burger() }}
          <nav class="nc-links" aria-label="Primary">{{ links() }}</nav>
        </div>
        <div class="n1__mid">{{ star("n1__star") }}{{ brand() }}{{ star("n1__star") }}</div>
        <div class="n1__side n1__side--r">
          <span class="n1__addr">247 Division St</span>
          <a class="btn btn--small n1__book" href="#" data-go="book">Book</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="n1__menu" data-menu>
      <nav aria-label="Mobile">{% for s in sections %}<a href="#" data-go="{{ s.id }}" style="--i:{{ loop.index0 }}">{{ s.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</nav>
      <p class="n1__menu-addr">247 Division St · Cobourg</p>
    </div>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 2 · Glass capsule ============ -->
<section class="nc-concept" id="c2" aria-labelledby="t2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nc-label">
      <span class="nc-label__tag">Concept 2</span>
      <h2 id="t2" class="nc-label__title">Glass capsule</h2>
      <p class="nc-label__text">A floating, frosted pill that never touches the edges. A soft highlight glides between links as you hover and rests on the section you're reading. Dark glass over the hero, ivory glass after. On a phone the pill opens into a rounded card.</p>
    </div>
    {% call stage("n2") %}
    <header class="nc-nav">
      <div class="n2__pill">
        {{ brand() }}
        <nav class="nc-links n2__links" aria-label="Primary"><span class="n2__ind" data-indicator aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ links() }}</nav>
        <a class="n2__book" href="#" data-go="book">Book</a>
        <button class="n2__menu-btn" type="button" data-menu-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="n2__menu-word">Menu</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
        <div class="n2__menu" data-menu>
          <div class="n2__menu-in">
            <nav aria-label="Mobile">{{ links() }}</nav>
            <a class="n2__book n2__book--wide" href="#" data-go="book">Book an appointment</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 3 · Front desk ============ -->
<section class="nc-concept" id="c3" aria-labelledby="t3">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nc-label">
      <span class="nc-label__tag">Concept 3</span>
      <h2 id="t3" class="nc-label__title">Front desk</h2>
      <p class="nc-label__text">A thin teal strip on top holds the practical things: address, directions, booking policy, Facebook. Below it, the familiar bar. On scroll the strip tucks away and the bar goes solid, with the current section underlined. On a phone a teal panel slides in from the right.</p>
    </div>
    {% call stage("n3") %}
    <header class="nc-nav">
      <div class="n3__strip">
        <span>247 Division St, Cobourg · <a href="#" data-go="visit">Directions</a></span>
        <span class="n3__mid">Cuts · Colour · Styling · By appointment</span>
        <a class="n3__fb" href="#">Facebook</a>
      </div>
      <div class="n3__bar">
        {{ brand() }}
        <nav class="nc-links" aria-label="Primary">{{ links() }}</nav>
        <a class="btn btn--small n3__book" href="#" data-go="book">Book</a>
        {{ burger() }}
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="n3__menu" data-menu>
      <nav aria-label="Mobile">{% for s in sections %}<a href="#" data-go="{{ s.id }}" style="--i:{{ loop.index0 }}"><span>0{{ loop.index }}</span>{{ s.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</nav>
      <div class="n3__menu-foot">
        <a class="btn btn--light" href="#" data-go="book">Book an appointment</a>
        <p>247 Division St · Cobourg<br />By appointment</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 4 · The index ============ -->
<section class="nc-concept" id="c4" aria-labelledby="t4">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nc-label">
      <span class="nc-label__tag">Concept 4</span>
      <h2 id="t4" class="nc-label__title">The index</h2>
      <p class="nc-label__text">Very little on screen: wordmark, Book, and a “Menu” button. The bar hides while you scroll down and comes back the moment you scroll up. Menu opens a teal index of big numbered links; hovering one shows its photo in an arch. Desktop and phone work the same way.</p>
    </div>
    {% call stage("n4") %}
    <header class="nc-nav">
      {{ brand() }}
      <a class="link n4__book" href="#" data-go="book">Book</a>
      <button class="n4__menu-btn" type="button" data-menu-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="n4__word" data-open="Menu" data-close="Close"></span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
    </header>
    <div class="n4__panel" data-menu>
      <nav class="n4__list" aria-label="Index">
        {%- for s in sections %}<a href="#" data-go="{{ s.id }}" data-key="{{ s.id }}" style="--i:{{ loop.index0 }}"><span>0{{ loop.index }}</span>{{ s.label }}</a>{% endfor -%}
      </nav>
      <div class="n4__preview" aria-hidden="true">
        <img class="is-on" data-preview="services" src="/assets/img/services/colour.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="" />
        <img data-preview="studio" src="/assets/img/studio-detail.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="" />
        <img data-preview="gallery" src="/assets/img/lookbook/movement-thumb.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="" />
        <img data-preview="visit" src="/assets/img/storefront.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="" />
      </div>
      <div class="n4__foot"><span>247 Division St · Cobourg</span><span>By appointment</span><a href="#">Facebook</a></div>
    </div>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 5 · Booking dock ============ -->
<section class="nc-concept" id="c5" aria-labelledby="t5">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nc-label">
      <span class="nc-label__tag">Concept 5</span>
      <h2 id="t5" class="nc-label__title">Booking dock</h2>
      <p class="nc-label__text">No bar at the top at all: the wordmark floats free and inverts against whatever's behind it. The links live in a teal dock at the bottom, with a coral line tracking how far down the page you are. On a phone the dock becomes three thumb-sized buttons (Menu, Directions, Book) and the menu rises as a sheet.</p>
    </div>
    {% call stage("n5") %}
    {{ brand("n5__brand") }}
    <span class="n5__corner" aria-hidden="true">247 Division St</span>
    <div class="n5__scrim" data-menu-close></div>
    <div class="n5__sheet" data-menu>
      <span class="n5__handle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <nav aria-label="Mobile">{% for s in sections %}<a href="#" data-go="{{ s.id }}" style="--i:{{ loop.index0 }}">{{ s.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</nav>
      <p class="n5__sheet-addr">247 Division St · Cobourg · By appointment</p>
    </div>
    <nav class="n5__dock" aria-label="Primary">
      <span class="n5__links">{{ links() }}</span>
      <button class="n5__m" type="button" data-menu-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Menu</button>
      <a class="n5__m" href="#" data-go="visit">Directions</a>
      <a class="n5__book" href="#" data-go="book">Book</a>
    </nav>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ Comparison ============ -->
<section class="nc-compare" id="compare" aria-labelledby="tc">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Side by side</p>
    <h2 id="tc" class="h2">At a glance</h2>
    <div class="nc-table-wrap">
      <table class="nc-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Concept</th><th scope="col">Feels like</th><th scope="col">Strongest at</th><th scope="col">Watch out for</th><th scope="col">Build effort</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row"><span>1</span>Shopfront</th><td>Classic boutique, signage</td><td>Brand presence; balanced and calm</td><td>Centre logo competes with the hero headline; needs 4 links max</td><td><i class="nc-dots" style="--n:2"></i>Low</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><span>2</span>Glass capsule</th><td>Modern, light, app-like</td><td>Feels premium; never blocks the hero edges</td><td>Blur costs a little on older phones; can read as “tech”</td><td><i class="nc-dots" style="--n:3"></i>Medium</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><span>3</span>Front desk</th><td>Practical, local, trustworthy</td><td>Address and booking info up front; good for local SEO and first-timers</td><td>Busiest at the top; strip needs real hours and a phone number</td><td><i class="nc-dots" style="--n:2"></i>Low</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><span>4</span>The index</th><td>Editorial, magazine</td><td>Most screen for photos; the menu itself becomes a moment</td><td>Links hidden behind a click on desktop; one extra step to find things</td><td><i class="nc-dots" style="--n:3"></i>Medium</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><span>5</span>Booking dock</th><td>Bold, thumb-first</td><td>Book is always one tap away on phones; most distinctive</td><td>Unusual on desktop; dock covers the bottom of content</td><td><i class="nc-dots" style="--n:4"></i>Higher</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="nc-compare__note"><strong>Mix and match:</strong> these are separable. The Front desk strip, the Glass capsule's gliding highlight, or the Booking dock's phone bar could each be added to the current nav on their own.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="/assets/js/nav-concepts.js" defer></script>
